It is our responsibility to ensure that Michigan’s firefighters and front-line responders have the resources they need to keep our communities safe.

@SenGaryPeters and I welcome $700,000 in federal funding for local fire departments in Muskegon, Ross Augusta, Marengo Township, Norton Shores, Hudsonville and across the state.

We’ve worked in a bipartisan way to secure this essential grant funding. These dollars will help departments purchase new fire hoses, air tanks, a brush truck, vehicle exhaust removal systems, and personal protective equipment for new cadets — providing firefighters with the equipment they need to protect Michiganders every day.

